From 93be6655f31747eb6af21caaab6ff83c1b19bf36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:15:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Cases run with the float numerical type

- The MPI reductions and gathers of real values use the MPI type of
  mfem_mgis::real instead of MPI_DOUBLE (macroscopic stress, bubble
  post-processings), and the option --duration of the cermet case is a
  mfem_mgis::real, as MFEM expects.
- The loop computing the Kroener shear modulus stops when the relative
  change is below 1e-10 or ten times the machine epsilon of
  mfem_mgis::real, instead of 1e-10 which can't be reached in float.
- The absolute tolerance of the microscopic equilibrium is kept when the
  criterion is switched (it is null by default with double). With float,
  the residual of the polycrystal and cermet cases stagnates at about 6e3
  whatever the loading (the deformation gradient, close to the identity,
  is rounded to about 1e-7): its default is ten times this floor.
- The bubble case, elastic and solved in one iteration, uses a relative
  tolerance of 1e-4 with float (2.8e-5 measured).
- run-and-check.py compares the times of the rows up to 1e-6, the time
  0.2 being written 0.20000000298023 with float.

Double: the 6 CPU tests pass with the same output files, to the bit.
Float (MFEM precision=single): the 6 tests pass; the axial stresses
differ from the double ones by 0.06 % to 0.15 %, and from the Cast3M
references by 0.005 % to 0.23 %.
